   "daf": "32a",
   "sentenceId": 12,
   "he": "צִינֵּי הַר הַבַּרְזֶל — כְּשֵׁרָה. אָמַר אַבָּיֵי: לֹא שָׁנוּ אֶלָּא שֶׁרֹאשׁוֹ שֶׁל זֶה מַגִּיעַ לְצַד עִיקָּרוֹ שֶׁל זֶה, אֲבָל אֵין רֹאשׁוֹ שֶׁל זֶה מַגִּיעַ לְצַד עִיקָּרוֹ שֶׁל זֶה — פָּסוּל.",
   "en": "§ The mishna continues: A lulav from the «palms of the Iron Mountain is fit.» It has few leaves on its spine, and those leaves are not crowded together like the leaves on a standard lulav. «Abaye said:» The Sages «taught that» this type of lulav is fit «only» in a case in which «the top of this» leaf «reaches the base of that» leaf above it on the spine. «However,» if there are so few leaves that «the top of this» leaf «does not reach the base of that» leaf, «it is unfit.»"
  }
 ],
